---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe1506.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Three Distinct Categories of Change" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Accounting Policy Changes Required by a New or Amended Section" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Voluntary Accounting Policy Changes" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Changes in Accounting Estimates — Prospective Application" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Distinguishing a Policy Change From an Estimate Change" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Correction of Prior Period Errors — Retrospective Restatement" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Materiality of an Error" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — a Voluntary Accounting Policy Change" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example — Correcting a Material Prior Period Error" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IAS 8" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Three genuinely different treatments for three genuinely different situations</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 1506 governs HOW an ENTERPRISE accounts FOR changes IN accounting POLICIES, changes IN accounting ESTIMATES, and CORRECTIONS of PRIOR period ERRORS — THREE genuinely DIFFERENT situations, EACH requiring a DIFFERENT accounting TREATMENT, STRUCTURALLY parallel to IAS 8 internationally and ASBE No. 28 (see the COMPANION Chinese GAAP poster EARLIER in this LIBRARY).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Three Distinct Categories of Change</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Policy changes, estimate changes, and error corrections</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Treatment</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Accounting policy change</span><span>RETROSPECTIVE application (RESTATING comparatives), UNLESS a NEW Section'S OWN transition PROVISIONS specify OTHERWISE, or RETROSPECTIVE application IS impracticable</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Accounting estimate change</span><span>PROSPECTIVE application (NO restatement OF prior periods)</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Prior period error correction</span><span>RETROSPECTIVE restatement, FOR material ERRORS</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Accounting Policy Changes Required by a New or Amended Section</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Follow the new Section's own transitional provisions where specified</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE a NEW or AMENDED ASPE Section REQUIRES a CHANGE in ACCOUNTING policy, an ENTERPRISE applies the TRANSITIONAL provisions SPECIFIED within THAT Section — WHERE no SPECIFIC transitional GUIDANCE is PROVIDED, the CHANGE is applied RETROSPECTIVELY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Voluntary Accounting Policy Changes</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Only where the change results in more reliable and more relevant information</div><div class="text-supporting">A VOLUNTARY change IN accounting POLICY is PERMITTED only WHERE the CHANGE will RESULT in the FINANCIAL statements PROVIDING more RELIABLE and MORE relevant INFORMATION about the EFFECTS of TRANSACTIONS — a VOLUNTARY change is APPLIED retrospectively, AS IF the NEW policy had ALWAYS been APPLIED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Changes in Accounting Estimates — Prospective Application</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Adjusting future periods only, with no restatement</div><div class="text-supporting">A CHANGE in an ACCOUNTING estimate (e.g. a REVISED useful LIFE for PROPERTY, plant, and EQUIPMENT, or a REVISED bad DEBT allowance RATE) is applied PROSPECTIVELY — AFFECTING the CURRENT period and FUTURE periods ONLY, WITH NO restatement OF prior periods, SINCE the ORIGINAL estimate was REASONABLE based ON the information AVAILABLE at the TIME.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Distinguishing a Policy Change From an Estimate Change</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A key judgment with materially different consequences</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE it is DIFFICULT to DISTINGUISH a CHANGE in ACCOUNTING policy FROM a CHANGE in ACCOUNTING estimate, the CHANGE is TREATED as a CHANGE in ESTIMATE — a PRACTICAL default REFLECTING that MOST such AMBIGUOUS cases GENUINELY involve a REFINEMENT of JUDGMENT rather THAN a wholesale CHANGE in the UNDERLYING accounting PRINCIPLE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Correction of Prior Period Errors — Retrospective Restatement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Restating comparatives as if the error never occurred</div><div class="text-supporting">MATERIAL errors RELATING to PRIOR periods are CORRECTED retrospectively — RESTATING the COMPARATIVE amounts PRESENTED for the PRIOR period(s) in WHICH the ERROR occurred, AS IF the ERROR had NEVER been MADE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Materiality of an Error</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Only material errors require retrospective correction</div><div class="text-supporting">ONLY material ERRORS require RETROSPECTIVE restatement — an ERROR is MATERIAL if it COULD reasonably be EXPECTED to INFLUENCE the DECISIONS of USERS relying ON the FINANCIAL statements, ASSESSED both INDIVIDUALLY and IN aggregate WITH other ERRORS, CONSISTENT with the MATERIALITY concept INTRODUCED in Section 1000.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — a Voluntary Accounting Policy Change</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Restating comparatives for improved reliability</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Changing an inventory cost formula</div><div class="wk-body">A private company changes its inventory cost formula from FIFO to weighted average, determining this provides more reliable and relevant information about its inventory costs given a change in its purchasing pattern.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company APPLIES the NEW weighted AVERAGE formula RETROSPECTIVELY, RESTATING comparative FIGURES as IF weighted AVERAGE had ALWAYS been USED, DISCLOSING the NATURE of and REASON for the CHANGE per Section 1505.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Correcting a Material Prior Period Error</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Restating a comparative period to remove the error</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A previously omitted liability</div><div class="wk-body">A private company discovers that a material $250,000 liability was mistakenly omitted from the prior year's financial statements due to a clerical error.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company RESTATES the PRIOR year'S comparative FIGURES to INCLUDE the $250,000 LIABILITY (and its ASSOCIATED expense), CORRECTING the ERROR retrospectively, WITH appropriate DISCLOSURE of the NATURE of the ERROR and the AMOUNT of the CORRECTION.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 1506 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and reason for any accounting policy change, and its financial effect</span><span>Nature and amount of any change in accounting estimate affecting the current or future periods</span><span>Nature of any prior period error corrected, and the amount of the correction for each period presented</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Distinguishing a genuine accounting policy change from a change in estimate</span><span>Assessing whether an identified error is material</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Quantifying the financial effect of a policy change or error correction on prior periods</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 8</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 1506 vs IAS 8</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 1506</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 8</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Policy changes</span><span>Retrospective</span><span>Retrospective — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Estimate changes</span><span>Prospective</span><span>Prospective — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Error corrections</span><span>Retrospective restatement</span><span>Retrospective restatement — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard structurally, REFLECTING the SHARED conceptual FOUNDATIONS underlying BOTH the CANADIAN and INTERNATIONAL frameworks IN this area.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every category of change lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Policy change / error correction</span><span>ALL comparative statements</span><span>Retrospectively restated</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Estimate change</span><span>Current and future periods only</span><span>No restatement of prior periods</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1505</span><span>Disclosure of Accounting Policies — governs the ongoing disclosure of the policies this Section's change provisions modify</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1400</span><span>General Standards of Financial Statement Presentation — governs the comparative restatement this Section's retrospective provisions require</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Retrospective application</div><div class="glossary-def">Applying a new accounting policy or correcting an error as if it had always applied, restating comparative periods accordingly.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Prospective application</div><div class="glossary-def">Applying a change only to the current and future periods, without restating prior periods.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe1506 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
